invariant: INV-26
file: src/gcm.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: gcm_traffic_key_store computes the hash subkey and its powers whatever
  aes_traffic_key_store answered, so keying an AES-GCM suite runs the AES
  instructions and the carry-less multiply in a session whose caller did
  not set CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES, which runs neither otherwise (INV-26),
  and on a CPU without them it dies of SIGILL. It also answers 1, so the
  owner then reads a schedule nothing wrote. bin/aes_runtime_test keys a
  set under a value without the bit, requires stored at 0 and counts the
  calls of both kinds (docs/decisions.md 160 and 234).

--- old
    if (!aes_traffic_key_store(schedule, cpu, key, key_len)) {
        return 0;
    }
--- new
    (void)aes_traffic_key_store(schedule, cpu, key, key_len);
